   DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       llllvvmm--pprrooffddaattaa oovveerrllaapp takes two profile data  files  and  displays  the
       _o_v_e_r_l_a_p of counter distribution between the whole files and between any
       of the specified functions.

       In this command, _o_v_e_r_l_a_p is defined as follows:  Suppose  _b_a_s_e  _p_r_o_f_i_l_e
       _f_i_l_e  has the following counts: {c1_1, c1_2, ..., c1_n, c1_u_1, c2_u_2,
       ..., c2_u_s}, and _t_e_s_t _p_r_o_f_i_l_e _f_i_l_e has {c2_1, c2_2, ..., c2_n, c2_v_1,
       c2_v_2,  ..., c2_v_t}.  Here c{1|2}_i (i = 1 .. n) are matched counters
       and c1_u_i (i = 1 .. s) and c2_v_i (i = 1 .. v) are unmatched  counters
       (or counters only existing in) _b_a_s_e _p_r_o_f_i_l_e _f_i_l_e and _t_e_s_t _p_r_o_f_i_l_e _f_i_l_e,
       respectively.  Let sum_1 = c1_1 + c1_2 +  ... + c1_n +  c1_u_1 + c2_u_2
       +  ... + c2_u_s, and sum_2 = c2_1 + c2_2 + ... + c2_n + c2_v_1 + c2_v_2
       +  ...   +   c2_v_t.    _o_v_e_r_l_a_p   =   min(c1_1/sum_1,   c2_1/sum_2)   +
       min(c1_2/sum_1, c2_2/sum_2) + ...  + min(c1_n/sum_1, c2_n/sum_2).

       The  result  overlap  distribution is a percentage number, ranging from
       0.0% to 100.0%, where 0.0% means there is no overlap and 100.0% means a
       perfect overlap.

       Here  is an example, if _b_a_s_e _p_r_o_f_i_l_e _f_i_l_e has counts of {400, 600}, and
       _t_e_s_t _p_r_o_f_i_l_e _f_i_l_e has matched counts of {60000, 40000}. The _o_v_e_r_l_a_p  is
       80%.

